## 🎉 **Day 30 of 90 Days of Reinforcement Learning**

### **30 Days In — What I’ve Learned So Far**

Today marks the completion of the **first 30 days** of my Reinforcement Learning journey.  
Instead of introducing a new algorithm, I’m pausing to **reflect, consolidate, and zoom out**.

---

## 🧠 **What These 30 Days Covered**

### 🔹 Foundations
- Agent, Environment, State, Action, Reward  
- MDPs, Policies, Value Functions  
- Exploration vs Exploitation  

### 🔹 Classical RL
- Monte Carlo methods  
- Temporal Difference learning  
- SARSA vs Q-learning  

### 🔹 Deep RL
- Function approximation with neural networks  
- DQN and its improvements  
  - Double DQN  
  - Dueling DQN  
  - Prioritized Experience Replay  
  - Rainbow DQN  

### 🔹 Policy-Based & Actor–Critic Methods
- Policy Gradients & REINFORCE  
- Actor–Critic, A2C, A3C  
- PPO, TRPO  
- Soft Actor-Critic (SAC)  

### 🔹 Advanced Concepts
- Stability in policy optimization  
- Entropy & exploration  
- Model-Based Reinforcement Learning  

---

## 📌 **Key Lessons (More Important Than Algorithms)**

1️⃣ **Stability matters more than raw performance**  
2️⃣ **Exploration is not a side detail — it’s central to intelligence**  
3️⃣ **Small architectural ideas often outperform “big” new algorithms**  
4️⃣ **Deep RL is fragile without the right constraints**  
5️⃣ **Understanding *why* algorithms exist is more valuable than memorizing them**

---

## 🔭 **What’s Coming Next (Days 31–60)**

The next phase will go deeper into:
- Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning  
- Hierarchical RL  
- Safe RL & constraints  
- Sim-to-Real challenges  
- RL for robotics and real-world systems  

This is where theory starts meeting **real deployment challenges**.

